{
  "name": "Route Support Tickets into SLA Queues and Reply Drafts via Webhook",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "support-overview-note",
      "name": "Start Here",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1380,
        -720
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 650,
        "height": 430,
        "content": "## Production support triage\n\nThis workflow accepts a support ticket, validates it, assigns a queue and response SLA, writes a durable audit row, alerts the right team, optionally acknowledges the requester, and returns a structured webhook response.\n\n### Before activation\n\n1. Connect Google Sheets and Gmail credentials.\n2. Replace every `example.com` destination.\n3. Create the audit-sheet columns listed in the setup note.\n4. Test the valid and invalid sample payloads.\n5. Review categories, SLA hours, and message copy with the support owner."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "support-input-note",
      "name": "1. Input and Validation",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1260,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 620,
        "height": 230,
        "content": "## 1. Receive and validate\n\nPOST JSON to the webhook with `subject` and `message`. Optional fields are `ticket_id`, `requester_name`, `requester_email`, `account_id`, `customer_tier`, and `source`.\n\nThe Set node normalizes common aliases. Missing subject or message returns HTTP 400 without logging or sending email."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "support-policy-note",
      "name": "2. Triage Policy",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -580,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 620,
        "height": 230,
        "content": "## 2. Classify and assign SLA\n\nThe policy node evaluates transparent keyword lists for account access, billing, sales, and technical issues. It separately calculates critical, high, normal, or low priority and a 1, 4, 12, or 24 hour target.\n\nEdit the arrays in this node to match your product language and support policy."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "support-audit-note",
      "name": "3. Audit Log Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        100,
        -620
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 720,
        "height": 250,
        "content": "## 3. Keep a durable audit trail\n\nCreate a Google Sheet tab named `Ticket audit` with these headers: `received_at`, `ticket_id`, `dedupe_key`, `requester_email`, `account_id`, `subject`, `category`, `priority`, `sla_hours`, `sla_due_at`, `owner_queue`, `source`, `matched_signals`, `message`.\n\nThe deterministic dedupe key makes repeat submissions easy to identify in the sheet or a downstream database."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "support-routing-note",
      "name": "4. Queue Routing",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        440,
        460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 760,
        "height": 240,
        "content": "## 4. Route by urgency and category\n\nCritical and high-priority tickets alert the on-call address first. Remaining tickets route to billing, sales, or general support. Replace the four placeholder destinations and tailor each message to the receiving team.\n\nEvery path converges before customer acknowledgment, so the webhook returns exactly once."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "support-response-note",
      "name": "5. Acknowledge and Return",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1240,
        460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 650,
        "height": 240,
        "content": "## 5. Close the loop\n\nWhen `requester_email` is present, Gmail sends a plain-language acknowledgment with the ticket ID, category, priority, and SLA target. Without an email, the workflow skips that message.\n\nThe final webhook payload always keeps `requires_human_review: true`; no AI-generated response is sent automatically."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "support-ticket-webhook",
      "name": "Support Ticket Webhook",
